+# TASK-260830-8x76g1 developer recovery logbook
+
+## Decisions and findings
+
+1. The two supplied archives were treated as read-only authority. Their hashes matched, and overlay order was accepted leaves followed by audit carryforward.
+2. The workspace also contained later task files (`constraint_inventory_test.go`, `performance_test.go`, and the enumeration artifact). After archive overlay, they exposed a real expected-red mismatch against the older recovered production validator.
+3. Rather than re-derive hundreds of constraints, the run materialized the board-owned CR revision 8 patch and reconstructed `HEAD + patch` in `.temp/`. Clean patch applicability and byte identity across all 69 paths bind the tested workspace to that candidate.
+4. The first source-binding loops were invalid because a zsh loop variable named `path` overwrote zsh's special `$path` array, causing command lookup failures. Those loops are excluded from evidence. The corrected loop used `artifact_path`, found `/usr/bin/cmp`, failed closed on any mismatch, and exited 0.
+5. The first configured format gate exited 1 because a reviewer probe under `.temp/TASK-260830-8x76g1/review/overlap-probe/main.go` was unformatted. `gofmt -l .` named only that task-local scratch file. Formatting that scratch made the exact configured gate exit 0; repository candidate bytes remained bound to CR revision 8.
+6. `task-board validate` exited 0 while reporting 262 inherited `MISSING_ACTIVITY` diagnostics. `TASK-260830-8x76g1` does not occur in that validation log.
+7. No operator directives were recorded at the pre-handoff checkpoint.
+
+## Tool readiness
+
+- `task-board 0.24.3-174-g3998c779`: status/read/resource operations succeeded.
+- `git 2.50.1`: status, archive, patch, diff and binding operations succeeded.
+- `go1.25.5 darwin/arm64`: build, vet, tests, race, coverage, fuzz and cross-builds succeeded.
+- `bsdtar 3.5.3`: both supplied archives listed/extracted successfully.
+- `/usr/bin/cmp`: corrected byte-binding loop succeeded.
+
+## Scope boundary
+
+The candidate implements common scalar, canonical JSON, object-identity, and scoped Sections 10.1-10.4/17.3 traceability behavior only. It does not implement or advertise migration publication, atomic-reference behavior, or durable-state mutation.
