+# TASK-260830-8x76g1 developer recovery results
+
+Run: `RUN-260901-94588a`
+
+## Delivered candidate
+
+- Verified both supplied recovery inputs at the advertised SHA-256 digests:
+  - accepted leaves: `9ae5e624addc7d954c391d96cab7c9f7aac3e6bcee58c76dd0cc95533d0eac9c`
+  - audit carryforward: `df8d8fa712e0ce85bde4776dc1f83cef9d373593e76fd1145ce9d85b593ce4ee`
+- Restored the accepted leaves first and the audit carryforward second.
+- The carryforward deliberately exposed a red inventory gate: the per-member artifact contained 45 Session Record and nested members for which the recovered production file no longer contained `requireExactMembers` calls. The focused test exited 1 before candidate recovery.
+- Materialized the already-published task-scoped `TASK-260830-8x76g1_change-request_rev8.patch`, applied it cleanly to `HEAD` in a temporary tree, and restored that exact candidate. All 69 patch paths are byte-identical between the temporary candidate and the Story workspace.
+
+## Production evidence
+
+- `CalculateObjectIdentity` and `VerifyObjectIdentity` converge through `prepareObjectIdentity`; `internal/canonicaljson/canonical.go:196` invokes `validateImmutableObjectShape` before calculating or verifying the self identity.
+- `immutableObjectShapeValidators` is total over the generated self-identity registry. Unsupported registered schemas explicitly refuse; `TestImmutableObjectShapeValidatorCompletenessRejectsDeletedRegisteredSchema` proves deletion narrows the gate and fails completeness.
+- Session Record 1.0.0 and all reachable nested closed types use exact-member checks. `TestConstraintEnumerationMatchesRequireExactMembers` derives every member from production `requireExactMembers` calls and requires a one-to-one row in `testdata/constraint-enumeration.md` with its call site and pinned-spec declaration.
+- Session Record `name` enforces `[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}`. Both public identity entries accept 64 characters and refuse 65, a leading hyphen, space, control character, and non-ASCII.
+- Transfer Manifest destination-case collision membership uses `simpleFoldKey` and a map, not a pairwise scan. The production calculation entry accepted a 65,536-entry manifest within the 5 MiB identity cap in `0.30s`, below the 2s regression threshold.
+- Native fuzz coverage includes scalar production entries, canonical round trips, identity representation invariance, and recursive closed-shape refusal. The committed corpus includes leap seconds, lowercase RFC3339, invalid dates, malformed UUIDs, Windows reserved names/wildcards, unpaired surrogates, duplicate/non-string map keys, unknown closed members, chunk invariant failures, and invalid Session Record shapes.
+- The work is read-only identity validation/canonicalization. It mutates no durable state, so crash/idempotency recovery evidence is not applicable. README does not claim migration publication or atomic-reference support.
+
+## Foreground validation ledger
+
+Every gate was a standalone foreground process. Logs are in the attached validation archive.
+
